{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "In Session feels like a natural next choice because blues guitar connects with what interested me in Clapton and Hendrix.",
    "A Fool To Care gives me a clear connection to Memphis: another Boz Scaggs album with the soulful blues feel I want to hear."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Tony Bennett/Bill Evans collection and the Mamas & the Papas compilation miss my current mood; vocal jazz and harmony-focused pop do not offer the guitar-led blues feel I am seeking.",
    "Blues and Original Album Series leave me unsure about the music because I cannot identify the artist or contents, so I would not choose them on their titles alone."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat an interest in classic rock as a broad interest in familiar older music, though the sound matters more to me than the era.",
    "A greatest-hits collection or deluxe classic album is not automatically appealing just because I have listened to established artists."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The strongest connection for me right now is expressive blues guitar and soulful roots music, rather than classic rock in general.",
    "I rarely choose several albums in one visit, so a plausible connection is not enough; I need a specific reason as strong as the blues collaboration or the connection to Memphis."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my blues and roots-rock interests, but stretch them too broadly into older music without enough connection to my current listening mood."
}"}
